{
  "id": "terminal-courses",
  "questionId": "terminal-courses",
  "slug": "terminal-courses",
  "title": "Courses Nothing Depends On",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Topological sort",
  "patterns": [
    "topological sort",
    "graph",
    "out-degree"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "blind-75",
    "grind-75",
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "a course is terminal if it never shows up as the second element of any prerequisite pair - how would you track that in one pass?",
    "make a boolean array of size n, and for every prerequisite pair mark the second element as 'referenced'",
    "after one pass over all edges, which indices were never marked?",
    "collect those indices in ascending order - a left-to-right scan over the array already visits them in order"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "confusing which element of the pair is the dependent course and which is the prerequisite",
    "forgetting that a self-loop prerequisite marks that course as referenced, excluding it from the result",
    "not returning the result in ascending order"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There are `n` courses, labeled 0 to n - 1, and a list of prerequisite pairs `prereqs`, where each pair [a, b] means course a requires course b to be completed first (so b is a prerequisite for a).\n\n**Return, in ascending order, every course that is never listed as a prerequisite for any other course, meaning nothing depends on it.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= n <= 2000",
      "0 <= prerequisites.length <= 5000",
      "prerequisites[i].length == 2",
      "0 <= a, b < n for each [a, b] in prerequisites"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "no prerequisite edges at all - every course is terminal",
      "a self-loop prerequisite like [0, 0] means that course IS listed as a prerequisite (of itself), so it's not terminal",
      "a course that is a prerequisite for several other courses at once",
      "a straight dependency chain, where only the very last course in the chain is terminal"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "n = 4, prereqs = [[1, 0], [2, 0], [3, 1]]",
        "output": "[2, 3]",
        "expectedOutput": "[2, 3]",
        "explanation": "course 0 is a prerequisite for 1 and 2, and course 1 is a prerequisite for 3; courses 2 and 3 are never a prerequisite for anything"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "n = 3, prereqs = []",
        "output": "[0, 1, 2]",
        "expectedOutput": "[0, 1, 2]",
        "explanation": "with no prerequisite pairs at all, no course is ever required by another"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "n = 5, prereqs = [[2, 0], [2, 1], [4, 3]]",
        "output": "[2, 4]",
        "expectedOutput": "[2, 4]",
        "explanation": "courses 0, 1, and 3 are each a prerequisite for something; courses 2 and 4 are not"
      }
